Yes, 3 Kirk Brae is within the **Glenarrow Town Centre** conservation area. It is not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

Our guidance says replacement windows in a conservation area need planning permission unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. So:

- If you're replacing like-for-like (same material, such as timber, and the same glazing pattern and opening style), you may not need an application.
- If the material, design, or glazing pattern is changing (for example, uPVC instead of timber, or different glazing bars or opening style), you will need to apply.

I can't give a formal opinion on your specific proposal from the photo. If you tell me the existing and proposed materials and designs, I can help you judge whether it likely falls within the exception, but the council's decision is what counts. If you'd like, I can also look up any existing application reference for the property.
